00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:28.200
I mean, I watched my father
die like right before me.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:30.750
It's a scary thing. They
just stop breathing.

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:33.300
And just the idea of, like, nothing

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:35.910
is just extremely terrifying to me.

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:37.950
It's like, you don't really
know what's going on.

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:39.570
Like, are you even thinking,
are you even there?

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:42.750
You're just a blip out of just space.

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:46.050
- It is terrifying. You, we don't know.

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:47.940
And as a Christian, I want
to pretend that, like,

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:49.770
I know that there's, you
know, heaven and hell,

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:52.330
but at the end of the day,
I genuinely don't know.

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:55.110
- Yeah. I think I was always had the fear

00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:57.750
as a kid growing up that,
you know, I'm gonna die,

00:10:57.750 --> 00:10:59.430
and, like, not fulfill, like,

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:01.770
what I wanted to do here on Earth, right?

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:03.240
But every time I thought about dying

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:06.300
it was as an old person.

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:09.540
But two years ago when I
started working as a lifeguard,

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:12.060
this lady and her friend came
to the pool, and, you know,

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:13.260
I have the music going and everything.

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:14.880
She just starts having a seizure.

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:17.550
And luckily, you know,
I did everything right,

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:20.310
and EMS showed up, and she was safe.

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:22.530
But then two weeks later
she, unfortunately,

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:26.310
had another seizure while
driving, and she died.

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:29.360
And that's when I realized life is, like,

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:31.170
it can happen to anyone at any point.

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:34.230
And if I just die and don't
do anything with my life,

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:35.823
then that's what I'm scared of.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:41.850
- I said that I don't fear death
because I, unlike you guys,

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:44.310
I don't really have an experience,

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:46.830
so much hands-on experience with death.

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:49.470
- Am I afraid of the fact
that I will die someday?

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:54.470
No, but I think, you
know, obviously the fact

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:57.720
that it might come way
sooner than you expect

00:11:57.720 --> 00:11:59.790
is a scary thought.

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:04.790
But, like, it's the one
thing that makes life, like,

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:06.628
special, you know what I mean?

00:12:06.628 --> 00:12:08.400
It's the one thing I feel like

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:10.650
that actually gives meaning to it.

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:11.610
'Cause if you would never die

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:13.500
then you would never
do anything, you know?

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.248
Yeah, 'cause you would always
have more time to do it.

00:12:15.248 --> 00:12:18.750
(intense boom) (countdown beeping)

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:20.550
- Do you guys feel like
you can actually be

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:23.280
your genuine self when you're,
like, talking to a girl

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:24.570
or hanging out with a girl?

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:26.000
- There's definitely
difference between, like,

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:29.670
talking or opening up to like
my friends that are girls

00:12:29.670 --> 00:12:31.650
versus like a girl that I'm interested in.

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:33.300
- Like, obviously, if you're
trying to impress a girl

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:34.350
you're gonna be dressed nicely.

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:35.190
You're gonna wear some cologne,

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.007
and you're not gonna, like,
fight around her, right?

00:12:37.007 --> 00:12:38.970
It's like, it's a filter thing.

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:40.830
But, like, when it comes to your mom,

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:43.320
like your mom's a girl, and I
wholeheartedly trust my mom.

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:47.160
So I'm gonna be myself around
the people I trust more.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.030
- I guess that's what it is.

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:49.890
I just, there's a lot of times I walk away

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:51.447
with talking to a girl
I'm really interested in,

00:12:51.447 --> 00:12:52.740
and I'm like, "Man, I wasn't just,

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:54.327
I didn't just go up and be me."

00:12:54.327 --> 00:12:55.680
And then my best friend, right?

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:57.840
He's or not my, he used
to be my best friend.

00:12:57.840 --> 00:12:58.950
He's kind of a womanizer,

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:01.620
but I see him get so much
like, you know, success.

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:03.480
And every time I've gotten
success is doing things

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:05.130
that he's done, which is just putting

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:07.380
on facade, and telling them
what they want to hear.

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:10.320
- I think it's good to be
yourself because, I mean,

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:12.270
you can only put a mask on for so long.

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:15.810
- It's refreshing to talk
to people and realize that

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:18.120
I'm not the only one who feels
a certain way about things.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:22.320
It is, it's nice, and it's a
step in the right direction

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:24.390
for me in becoming more comfortable

00:13:24.390 --> 00:13:27.000
with being open and honest with everybody.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.070
- I think just the
whole open conversation,

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:31.200
like, this won't bite me in the end later

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:33.517
or, like, someone's not gonna
listen to this and think,

00:13:33.517 --> 00:13:34.830
"Oh, that guy's bad."

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:37.535
I have more safety of
expressing my honest opinions

00:13:37.535 --> 00:13:40.740
and, whether those be good
opinions or bad opinions,

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:43.980
it's like, it's a better way
to express one's true self

00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:46.740
without trying to be influenced
by what high school is.

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:48.750
And all the people
influencing you in high school

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:51.900
because, frankly, high school
is just popular culture.

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:53.350
What people think is popular.

00:13:54.210 --> 00:13:55.364
- [Interviewer] Thank you so much.

00:13:55.364 --> 00:13:58.031
